hpc:Memorylimittype a owl:Class .
hpc:JobMemoryLimit a MemoryLimitType .
hpc:ProcessMemoryLimit a MemoryLimitType .
hpc:TaskMemoryLimit a MemoryLimitType .
hpc:ProcessJobMemoryLimit a MemoryLimitType .
hpc:TaskJobMemoryLimit a MemoryLimitType .

hpc:enables a owl:ObjectProperty .

hpc:Jobmemorylimit rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Memorylimittype .
hpc:Processmemorylimit rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Memorylimittype .
hpc:Taskmemorylimit rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Memorylimittype .
hpc:Processjobmemorylimit rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Memorylimittype .
hpc:Taskjobmemorylimit rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Memorylimittype .

hpc:Enables rdfs:domain hpc:Memorylimittype ;
                                rdfs:range hpc:Memorylimittype .


For the MIG property, it is not clear from the provided documentation whether it is a part of the MemoryLimitType ontology or a separate concept. If it is part of the MemoryLimitType ontology, you can model it as follows:

hpc:mig a owl:DatatypeProperty .
hpc:Mig rdfs:domain hpc:Memorylimittype ;
                          rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .


If MIG is a separate concept, you can model it as follows:

hpc:Mig a owl:Class .
hpc:Mig rdfs:subClassOf owl:DatatypeProperty .
hpc:Mig rdfs:domain hpc:Job .
hpc:Mig rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
